% Figura (bloque 3, «Aversión a las pérdidas»): aversión al riesgo de segundo orden frente a aversión a las pérdidas de primer orden
% ante una misma apuesta pequeña, ganar o perder h al cincuenta por ciento.
% (a) Utilidad esperada (curva suave, vista de cerca): u = ln x alrededor de w = 10 con h = 1 (dibujo: x_d = 1,5 (x - 8,5);
%     y_d = 10 (ln x - 2,1)): ganancia ln 11 - ln 10 = 0,0953 y pérdida ln 10 - ln 9 = 0,1054, casi iguales.
% (b) Teoría de las perspectivas (función de valor de b3_funcion_valor, vista cerca del origen): v(1) = 0,725; v(-1) = -1,631
%     (lambda = 2,25). Escala 1,2; desplazada 2,8 cm hacia arriba para alinear los ejes horizontales de abajo.
% (c) Coste del riesgo en función del tamaño de la apuesta: segundo orden, 0,25 h^2; primer orden, 0,6 h (esquemático).
% Generar con: bash Code/generar_figura.sh b3_orden_aversion
\begin{tikzpicture}[font=\footnotesize, >={Stealth[length=4pt]}]
  % ---------------- (a) Curva suave ----------------
  \node[font=\footnotesize\bfseries] at (2.25,5.0) {(a) Utilidad esperada: curva suave};
  \draw[->] (0,0) -- (4.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
  \draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,3.8) node[above] {$u(x)$};
  \draw[very thick, domain=8.6:11.4, samples=40] plot ({1.5*(\x-8.5)}, {10*(ln(\x)-2.1)});
  \fill (0.75,0.9722) circle (1.5pt); \fill (2.25,2.0259) circle (1.5pt); \fill (3.75,2.9790) circle (1.5pt);
  \draw[dashed] (0.75,0.9722) -- (0.75,0) node[below] {$w-h$};
  \draw[dashed] (2.25,2.0259) -- (2.25,0) node[below] {$w$};
  \draw[dashed] (3.75,2.9790) -- (3.75,0) node[below] {$w+h$};
  \draw[dashed] (0,2.0259) -- (2.25,2.0259);
  \draw[dashed] (0,0.9722) -- (0.75,0.9722);
  \draw[dashed] (0,2.9790) -- (3.75,2.9790);
  \draw[decorate, decoration={brace, amplitude=3pt}] (-0.12,2.0259) -- (-0.12,2.9790) node[midway, left=3pt] {ganancia};
  \draw[decorate, decoration={brace, amplitude=3pt}] (-0.12,0.9722) -- (-0.12,2.0259) node[midway, left=3pt] {pérdida};
  % ---------------- (b) Pliegue ----------------
  \node[font=\footnotesize\bfseries] at (7.6,5.0) {(b) Perspectivas: pliegue};
  \begin{scope}[xshift=7.4cm, yshift=2.8cm, x=1.2cm, y=1.2cm]
    \draw[->] (-1.9,0) -- (1.9,0) node[right] {$x$};
    \draw[->] (0,-2.3) -- (0,1.3) node[above] {$v(x)$};
    \draw[very thick, domain=0:1.6, samples=30] plot (\x, {2*(1-exp(-0.45*\x))});
    \draw[very thick, domain=-1.55:0, samples=30] plot (\x, {-2.25*2*(1-exp(0.45*\x))});
    \fill (1,0.725) circle (1.5pt); \fill (-1,-1.631) circle (1.5pt);
    \draw[dashed] (1,0.725) -- (1,0) node[below] {$h$};
    \draw[dashed] (-1,-1.631) -- (-1,0) node[above] {$-h$};
    \draw[dashed] (0,0.725) -- (1,0.725);
    \draw[dashed] (0,-1.631) -- (-1,-1.631);
    \draw[decorate, decoration={brace, amplitude=3pt, mirror}] (1.12,0) -- (1.12,0.725) node[midway, right=3pt] {ganancia};
    \draw[decorate, decoration={brace, amplitude=3pt}] (0.12,-1.631) -- (0.12,0) node[midway, right=3pt] {pérdida};
  \end{scope}
  % ---------------- (c) Coste del riesgo ----------------
  \node[font=\footnotesize\bfseries] at (12.9,5.0) {(c) Coste del riesgo};
  \begin{scope}[xshift=11.3cm]
    \draw[->] (0,0) -- (3.4,0) node[below left] {$h$};
    \draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,3.8) node[above] {coste};
    \draw[very thick, domain=0:3.0, samples=40] plot (\x, {0.25*\x*\x});
    \node[anchor=west] at (3.05,2.3) {segundo orden};
    \draw[very thick, gray, domain=0:3.0] plot (\x, {0.6*\x});
    \node[gray, anchor=west] at (3.05,1.75) {primer orden};
  \end{scope}
\end{tikzpicture}
